# Draft:Kingsbridge Road station (New York, Westchester and Boston Railway)

----
}}
The Kingsbridge Road is an abandoned station on the New York, Westchester and Boston Railway (NYW&B) and is located after Eastchester–Dyre Avenue station in the Eastchester neighborhood of the Bronx, but is geographically located in Westchester. The station was close to where the IRT Dyre Avenue Line layup tracks are currently.The station opened in 1912 along with the New York, Westchester and Boston Railway. It had two side platforms and four tracks. It was closed in 1937, following the end of NYW&B operations. As of 2022 the former stairs have been bricked up, and the abutment remains.
